From 4e8debfffc04fda5cb966e4a61375f98f25183b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:35:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/53] B70-V7-PLEG: RAM-native INT8 PLE producer on the
 device, in the graph (B70_PLE_DEVICE_GATHER=1)

The host-prepared producer blocks on a D2H of the step's tokens (behind the
drafter), hashes and gathers on the host and copies up before every replay:
0.8 ms/step at c=1, 1.0-1.4 ms at c=8-12 with the GPU idle (B70_PHASE_TIMING,
on the deployed engine). It cannot be overlapped from the host: the verify rows are the drafter's
last output and the consumer is inlined into the FULL graph. Here the fused
Triton n-gram hash (ple_ngram_ids) and a Triton gather over the pinned slabs'
UVA device views run inside the forward next to the consumer; owned slots get
their 164-B rows, all others and rows past the actual tokens zeros, as the
host stage. prepare_inputs no longer syncs for PLE. The first real step runs
both paths and compares the bytes once (raises on a difference).
